  "notes": [
    "A WebSocket connection opens with an HTTP GET handshake, so the client's connect is an http link to the endpoint path (contract GET /path); its server is the addEndpoint(...) line of registerStompEndpoints, with the method's declaration as an alternative.",
    "STOMP frames are messaging links, producer to consumer. A client SEND to /app/x (the application destination prefix from setApplicationDestinationPrefixes) is consumed by @MessageMapping(\"/x\"); a reply via @SendTo(\"/topic/y\") is produced by the annotated method and consumed by the client's subscribe('/topic/y'). Destinations are written in full, prefix included.",
    "Every REST URL is `${serverApiUrl}api/...` with serverApiUrl = SERVER_API_URL, which angular.json and build-plugins/define-esbuild.ts define as ''. The relative URL resolves against <base href=\"/\"> in index.html, so the path is /api/....",
    "Services keep the base in a field (resourceUrl, infoUrl); httpResource(() => ({url: this.resourceUrl, params})) is a GET of that URL. client.line is the line holding the method name (.get/.post/...), or httpResource<.",
    "The WebSocket URL is '/websocket/tracker', set in buildUrl() (client_url_def) and passed through Location.prepareExternalUrl (base href '/'); the connect is webSocketFactory: () => SockJS(this.buildUrl()), SockJS called without new.",
    "No application destination prefix is set, so a SEND to /topic/activity reaches @MessageMapping(\"/topic/activity\") (and the simple broker). /topic/tracker has two producers: @SendTo on sendActivity and convertAndSend in the disconnect listener.",
